  "Id": 2859,
  "Title": "AKU-ISMC's Talha Murat Pursuing a PhD in History",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "AKU-ISMC's student, Talha Murat, has been accepted by Freie Universit\u00e4t Berlin \u200bto further his studies.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClassCC527C7DBE724FA488C4A1B89023D17C\"><p>\u200b<br>We warmly congratulate or student Talha Murat\u200b on being accepted by&#160;Freie Universit\u00e4t Berlin&#160;\u200bto undertake a&#160;PhD in History\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b and pursue his research interests.\u200b<br></p><p>Sharing his thoughts on this big achievement and the&#160;educational journey, Talha said&#58;&#160;&quot;After completing my MA in Turkish Studies, with particular focus on late Ottoman history, at Sabanc\u0131 University, Turkey, I wanted to broaden my knowledge in Islamic studies and improve my language skills to accomplish my own research aims at a PhD level. Hence, I decided to pursue another MA degree in London. The MA in Muslim Cultures at the Aga Khan University\u2019s Institute for the Study of Muslim Civilisations (AKU-ISMC) has perfectly aligned with my academic plans and goals, and the Arabic language programme being offered has increased my motivation with its intensive and helpful&#160;courses.&#160;\u200b<br></p><p>&quot;Indeed, the various courses and seminars I attended here have prepared me fully and provided me with the tools and knowledge needed to move to the next step. Also,&#160;at AKU-ISMC, I have been greatly supported by my supervisor Dr Walid Ghali as well as other faculty members. As a result of these immense efforts and support, I have been accepted to study a&#160;PhD in History at Freie Universit\u00e4t Berlin where I am planning to conduct a research on late Ottoman Sufism.&quot;<br></p></div>",
